UB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nEast Central Fremont County in central Colorado...\nNorthwestern Pueblo County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 600 PM MDT.\n\n* At 307 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1.25 to 2 inches in 1\nhour. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nPenrose.","ends":"2026-08-20T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Fremont, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d32aeb759a775eed3c809ac03e0b5c34ac0a8e7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d32aeb759a775eed3c809ac03e0b5c34ac0a8e7.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-20T19:01:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 201901 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 101 PM MDT Thu Aug 20 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Hot temperatures along with showers and thunderstorms expected each day through next Wednesday. - Sunday and Monday look to have the most widespread coverage, including flash flooding on area burn scars. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH FRIDAY NIGHT/... Issued at 1234 PM M","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-20T17:40:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 201740 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1140 AM MDT Thu Aug 20 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-211745- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Abov